                <pb facs="0741" n="647" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg647"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Taylor to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-10-24"><hi rendition="#italic">October 24, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received Nov. 7.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 580.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of the cablegram of the 15th instant.</p>
                <p>In my last interview with the minister for foreign affairs I duly presented this
                    matter to him according to your instructions.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hannis Taylor.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
